PART 2: ACCEPTABLE USE POLICY (AUP) FOR GENERATED OUTPUTS

As an explicit condition of being granted a license to execute and use this
software, you agree to the following terms regarding the ROMs and files
generated by the tool.

5.  ROM ATTRIBUTION & SYSTEM SIGNATURE CO-EXISTENCE Any Android ROM image,
    package, or firmware built, modified, patched, or ported using this software
    MUST comply with the following ethical guidelines: a) Visible Credit: Credit
    to the original tool ("CSM by Minhmc2077") must be visibly, accurately, and
    prominently included in all public release notes, forum threads, GitHub
    repositories, and social media posts. b) Signature Logic: If this tool is
    designed to inject a build signature (e.g., modifying ro.build.display.id in
    build.prop), you agree not to actively wipe or obfuscate this signature. If
    you modify the tool to append your own name, the final generated property
    value must preserve the original authorship in a co-existence format (e.g.,
    "Built by [YourName], powered by CSM by Minhmc2077").

6.  STRICT NON-COMMERCIAL USE OF OUTPUTS This software is provided exclusively
    to foster the personal, educational, and hobbyist Android community. You
    agree NOT to: a) Charge fees for any ROM ports or builds generated by this
    tool. b) Gate, hide, or restrict access to ROMs generated by this tool
    behind paywalls, subscriptions (e.g., Patreon, Ko-fi, Telegram Premium), or
    monetized/ad-shortened download links (e.g., AdFly, Linkvertise). c)
    Exception for Voluntary Donations: You are allowed to accept strictly
    voluntary donations. However, you MUST NOT force, mandate, or coerce users
    into donating to access the ROMs. Access to ROMs generated by this tool must
    remain 100% free and unconditionally accessible at all times.

